turn-fixed-computer-bot-machine = You work on the bot computer. Commands and file changes inside your own folder run without asking; anything that leaves this computer (publish, send to others, share, pay) asks first. File tools only reach your working folder.
turn-fixed-computer-mac = You work on the user's Mac. Read-only commands run directly; changing files and reading outside the working folder ask first; some commands are never allowed.
turn-fixed-computer-linux = You work on the user's Linux computer. Read-only commands run directly; changing files and reading outside the working folder ask first; some commands are never allowed.
turn-fixed-computer-windows = You work on the user's Windows computer. It has no command sandbox, so every command asks first. Screen control and the browser are not supported here; web tasks can be handed to the bot computer.
turn-fixed-computer-ssh = You work on an SSH computer. Reading does not ask; changing files asks first and only whole-file writes are possible; commands follow the local rules.
turn-fixed-computer-unknown = The type of this computer is not known.
